      "problem": "$3!\\,4!=$",
      "worked_solution": "The given expression is a product of two factorials.\n\n- Computing $3!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n3!=3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=6.\n$$\n\n- Computing $4!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n4!=4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=24.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3!\\,4! & =3!\\cdot 4! \\\\  & =6\\cdot 24 \\\\  & =144\\end{aligned}\n$$",
