      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Quotient of Factorials",
      "knowledge_point_uuid": "203386bf-cdf1-5a78-92fd-36fababfb971",
      "problem": "Evaluate $\\frac{11!}{8!}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that $11!=11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8!\\,.$ Then, we can cancel the $8!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11!}{8!} & =\\frac{11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8!}{8!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot \\cancel{8!}}{\\cancel{8!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9}{1} \\\\  & =990\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "source_bindings": [
